WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:11.900
In general, the transfer of data between Twinmotion and Unreal is rather straightforward, but in some cases, you may encounter some glitches that require your attention.

2
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.879
This is the case with the planters on the roof. Their LOD settings are quite aggressive.

3
00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:26.260
You'll also note that these planters are supposed to be identical and yet are using different static meshes for reference.

4
00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:30.750
Select the first planter using the Boxum static mesh reference.

5
00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:36.200
Open that reference in the static mesh editor by double-clicking its thumbnail.

6
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:49.710
Check the four existing LODs. Only the first two make sense.

7
00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:59.000
This is a low poly model we can do with just two LODs. Set the number of LODs to 2 and apply the changes.

8
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.989
Save the updates and exit the static mesh editor.

9
00:01:08.489 --> 00:01:12.890
Select all the planters and assign them to use the Boxum static mesh we just updated.

10
00:01:24.109 --> 00:01:26.510
Now they look better, even from afar.

11
00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:39.040
Similarly, you can make quick adjustments to collisions.

12
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:44.140
As mentioned, collisions are not carried over using Datasmith Interop.

13
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:53.560
You can test this by going into play mode and see that you can walk through walls.

14
00:01:54.900 --> 00:02:01.799
Fortunately with architectural scenes, walls are often made of simple geometry and usually have a low poly count.

15
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.450
This means that you can in fact use their geometry to detect collisions.

16
00:02:07.239 --> 00:02:14.139
To do it in bulk, you can filter all wall objects in the Outliner and press Enter to select them.

17
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.990
You can then right-click any of them and then use Browse to Asset.

18
00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.319
The associated assets are now selected in the Content Browser.

19
00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:36.460
Right-click on one of them and then choose Asset Actions, Edit Selection in Property Matrix.

20
00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:48.310
A dialog appears in the search box type Collision and then change the Collision Complexity to Use Complex Collision as Simple.

21
00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:16.639
For practice, do the same with the Curtain Panels actors to be able to collide with the curtain walls.

22
00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.800
Remember this method is only effective with simple geometry.

23
00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.500
With complex geometry, you would want to assign simple collision shells.

24
00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:36.180
Of course, your motion is now restricted inside the main building.

25
00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:50.599
In Twinmotion, the doors are made to open when you get close to them, but this effect has not made the transition to Unreal Engine.

26
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.860
In the next step, you replace the doors using a blueprint.
